{:edb/db-before-t 736 :edb/db-after-t 737 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534049 50 #inst "2026-10-06T01:16:57.243Z" 13194139534049 true] [17592186096527 1020 #edb/ref 17592186275999 13194139534049 true] [17592186096527 1020 #edb/ref 17592186276025 13194139534049 true] [17592186096529 1020 #edb/ref 17592186276006 13194139534049 true] [17592186096529 1020 #edb/ref 17592186276013 13194139534049 true] [17592186096530 1020 #edb/ref 17592186276018 13194139534049 true] [17592186275999 1017 #edb/ref 17592186276000 13194139534049 true] [17592186275999 1089 "q-107562" 13194139534049 true] [17592186275999 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534049 true] [17592186275999 1100 "Given that the expression $4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ)$ with ${0}^{∘}<ϕ<{90}^{∘}$ and $R>0$, what is the value of $ϕ?$" 13194139534049 true] [17592186275999 1113 #uuid "eb3f02cc-ae8b-5d22-af77-c5a4f4e69173" 13194139534049 true] [17592186275999 1145 "The sum formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=4 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ \\operatorna